Subject: [PATCH] Keep TLS handshake waiting in the cancellable external loop

Tachiai adaptation of OpenConnect 9.21 gnutls.c, 2026-10-09.
The TCP FD is already nonblocking. Tell GnuTLS not to wait internally under
its handshake timeout, so the existing command-FD select remains cancellable.
No protocol, certificate validation, cipher or trust changes.

--- a/gnutls.c
+++ b/gnutls.c
@@ -2362 +2362,2 @@
-	gnutls_init(&vpninfo->https_sess, GNUTLS_CLIENT|GNUTLS_FORCE_CLIENT_CERT);
+	/* Modified by Tachiai, 2026-10-09: keep command-pipe cancellation live. */
+	gnutls_init(&vpninfo->https_sess, GNUTLS_CLIENT|GNUTLS_FORCE_CLIENT_CERT|GNUTLS_NONBLOCK);
